  "body_html": "<h1>Kuhn Existence Of Pure Subgame-Perfect Equilibrium</h1>\n<p>Every finite perfect-information game, with or without Nature, has a\nsubgame-perfect equilibrium in pure strategies.</p>",
  "proof_html": "<p>Sketch</p>\n<p>Backward induction solves all terminal predecessor positions first. Replace each\nsuch position by the payoff generated by an optimal successor choice. The reduced\ntree is shorter, so induction gives a subgame-perfect strategy profile there.\nCombining the reduced-game strategy with the locally optimal choices at removed\npositions yields a pure strategy profile that is Nash in every subgame.</p>",
